Subject: [PATCH] i386: call void builtin generators without a destination

All VOID_FTYPE_VOID entries in bdesc_special_args use an instruction
generator taking no arguments. Passing an unused target selects the
one-operand function pointer in insn_gen_fn::operator(). WebAssembly
checks the indirect call signature and traps when expanding pause and
other void builtins in this group.

---
--- a/gcc/config/i386/i386-expand.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/i386/i386-expand.cc
@@ -14016,7 +14016,7 @@
   switch ((enum ix86_builtin_func_type) d->flag)
     {
     case VOID_FTYPE_VOID:
-      emit_insn (GEN_FCN (icode) (target));
+      emit_insn (GEN_FCN (icode) ());
       return 0;
     case VOID_FTYPE_UINT64:
     case VOID_FTYPE_UNSIGNED:
